  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 759181,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 1000 Mhz (Commodore 64) - Synopsis\n\nRelive the glory and challenge of the legendary 1000 Miglia rally in this pioneering Commodore 64 racing game! Set in 1927, *1000 Mhz* puts you behind the wheel of a classic 1930s race car as you tackle the grueling 1000-mile Italian route. Inspired by the real-world event, notorious for its difficulty and demanding setup, this game aims to capture the spirit of the original race.\n\nWhile boasting a distinctly arcade feel and somewhat limited sound quality, *1000 Mhz* stands out for its early attempt to simulate realistic car handling and behavior across varied racing conditions. Navigate winding roads, overcome challenging terrain, and manage your vehicle's performance to succeed.  Experience a unique blend of historical racing and arcade action, and discover why the creators initially believed this race – and this game – would be a one-off event! Prepare for a thrilling, albeit retro, rally experience."
    },
